# UI Design Rules (Light Mode Only)

## Tech Reference

- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router)
- UI Library: shadcn/ui
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Icons: Lucide React

## Design System & Theme

- Mode: Light mode ONLY.
- Theme System: Use standard shadcn semantic CSS variables (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `bg-accent`, `bg-muted`, etc.).
- Style: Clean, modern, minimal visual clutter, soft shadows, rounded corners (`rounded-xl`).

## UI Implementation Guidelines

- Focus strictly on clean UI design and visual layout structure.
- Always use shadcn/ui components (`Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, `Dialog`, etc.) instead of writing plain HTML.
- No hardcoded colors or sizes: Use Tailwind theme utilities (`text-sm`, `bg-primary`, `p-4`) instead of arbitrary values like `text-[15px]` or `bg-[#1e293b]`.
- Keep all layouts fully responsive out of the box using Tailwind flexbox and grid.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="bg-[#1e293b] text-[15px] px-[18px]">Apply</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<Button className="rounded-xl">Apply</Button>
<Card className="rounded-xl bg-card p-4 shadow-sm">
  <Badge variant="secondary">Full-time</Badge>
</Card>
```
